From: HSDH40C@prodigy.com ( STEVE B DENNETT)
Date: Mon, 21 Feb 1994 13:53:48 EST
Subject: [#94-2-198] GOAL: Reduce Sleep time

Anyone interested in reducing sleep time might want to check out the book
"Sleep less, live more" which came our a few (5? 8?) years ago.  It covered
most of the sleep research done up to that time, and talked about how to
reduce your sleep time as much as possible.  The technique was as follows:

1. establish a regular time for going to bed and waking in the morning, and
stick with it.

2. gradually reduce the total length of your sleep time (I believe the
recommendation was to decrease total sleep time by 30 minutes every 2 weeks).

3. keep doing this until you can reduce sleep time no further (ie., you are
having trouble staying awake the rest of the day).

4. reverse the process, gradually increasing the length of your sleep time
until the symptoms of sleep deprivation go away.

The authors claimed that test groups which followed this regime were able
to reduce their total sleep time from 1-5(?) hours per night, and that such
reductions persisted even a year later.

I don't have a copy of the book, and would be interested to hear if anyone
else out there does and can perhaps verify my recollection of the book's information.

-Steve


